.TH PHYLLO 1 "Phyllotaxis" "phyllo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
phyllo \- inspect and validate Phyllotaxis project integration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B phyllo
.B --help
.br
.B phyllo
.B --version
.br
.B phyllo
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phyllo
is a local, non-interactive integration CLI. Inspection does not install packages,
execute consumer configuration or lifecycle scripts, or mutate project files.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Validate the installed Venation contract. See
.BR phyllo-check (1).
.TP
.B status
Report discovered project, adapter, configuration, installed package, profile,
and Venation contract information.
.TP
.B doctor
Compose status inspection and canonical check without mutation.
.TP
.B init
Create a minimal declarative phyllotaxis.json file only if it does not already exist.
Use --dry-run to preview the exact proposed configuration.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show global usage on standard output; no consuming project is required.
.TP
.B --version
Show the invoked CLI package version, independent of the consumer package version.
.TP
.BI "command " --help
Show help for one implemented command.
.SH STRUCTURED OUTPUT
Commands with machine output use --format json; text is the default format. A JSON result includes schemaVersion,
command, ok, and diagnostics; command-specific data is optional.
Primary structured output goes to standard output. Process diagnostics go to standard error. Terminal presentation respects NO_COLOR, TERM=dumb, --no-color, and non-TTY output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful operation or valid requested contract.
.TP
.B 1
Contract validation found violations.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or configuration error.
.TP
.B 3
Operational failure.
.TP
.B 4
Unexpected internal CLI failure.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by SIGINT where the platform/runtime uses conventional signal propagation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B phyllotaxis.json
Optional inert, repository-local integration configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR phyllo-check (1)
.br
docs/cli/phyllo.md in the source repository documents the canonical command contract.
